# Companion Atlas — viewer-react configuration
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in.

# --- Photoreal globe (recommended) -----------------------------------------
# A Cesium ion access token (https://ion.cesium.com/tokens). With it the globe
# uses real World Imagery + World Terrain; without it, the bundled (low-res)
# Natural Earth II offline basemap is used, so the globe looks soft when zoomed.
VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# --- Connect to Companion Memory (CI-Server) -------------------------------
# Point the viewer at a CI-Server to render your real located memories instead
# of the bundled sample story. Overridable per-load with `?memory=<url>`.
#   e.g. http://localhost:3030  or  https://ci-server.localhost/api
VITE_MEMORY_URL=
# Optional Portal OIDC bearer token if the server doesn't accept the session
# cookie (also overridable with `?token=<jwt>`). Leave empty to rely on the
# signed-in session (fetch uses credentials: 'include').
VITE_MEMORY_TOKEN=

# The named-places layer (toggle in the top bar; CI-Server's `places`/
# `placesNear` API) reuses VITE_MEMORY_URL/VITE_MEMORY_TOKEN above — no
# separate config. Two operator-side prerequisites on the CI-Server this
# points at, neither of which this app can configure itself:
#   - CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS on CI-Server must include this app's origin.
#   - The signed-in session / token must be authorized for CI-Server's
#     PlaceResolver (JwtOrApiKeyAuthGuard — the same auth already required
#     for the memory layer above).
